# --- Research sub-modules ------------------------------------------------------
# The sub-module directories are tracked as gitlinks (mode 160000), and
# .gitignore has NO effect on them: a tracked path is never ignored. Patterns
# such as "napari/" here used to be dead weight.
#
# What actually keeps `git status` clean is `ignore = dirty` in .gitmodules:
#
#     [submodule "napari"]
#         ignore = dirty
#
# Without it, untracked files inside a sub-module are reported as
# "modified: napari (untracked content)". Inspect a sub-module with:
#
#     git -C <submodule> status
#
# Do NOT add unanchored patterns for directories that also occur inside the
# evidence packs: a bare "napari/" would also match
# "<project>-resultados/_evidence/napari/", silently hiding real evidence files.

# --- Python / TBO -------------------------------------------------------------
# General Python build artefacts (in case packaging happens in-tree).
# Root-anchored so they cannot swallow a nested directory of the same name
# inside an evidence pack.
/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
/build/
/dist/
/.venv/
/venv/
.coverage
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.hypothesis/

# --- Personal working copies ---------------------------------------------------
# TBO is the owner's own application. It used to be a sub-module of this
# repository; it is now an ordinary independent Git clone checked out here, so
# that it can be edited and pushed to its own remote without this repository
# recording a different commit every time.
#
# Ignored on purpose: its files must not be tracked here, and its Git history
# lives in PyQt6-Apps/TBO/.git, not in this repository.
#
#     git -C PyQt6-Apps/TBO status
#
# Anchored to the root so it cannot accidentally match a nested directory of the
# same name inside an evidence pack.
#
# lucio-iva-calculator is the same kind of tree: an independent clone of the
# owner's own application, read as a case study but never tracked here. It is
# also pinned as a sub-module *of TBO*, which is a different repository.
#
# Every pattern below is anchored. A bare "PyQt6-Apps/" used to sit here and it
# ignored the whole directory, which would have swallowed the two
# "<project>-resultados/" evidence folders that live beside the clones. That is
# the same mistake this file warns about at the top.
/PyQt6-Apps/TBO/
/PyQt6-Apps/lucio-iva-calculator/
/PyQt6-Apps/TBO-GitHub-Actions-Executables/
